{
  "description": "Type a missing object. Braintrust never answers 404 for an id it cannot find: observed live 2026-11-12 against api.braintrust.dev with a full-access service key, a random id (and, for projects and env vars, one just deleted) fails with a message that names both causes, under a status and content type that vary by resource and method. GET mostly answers 403 JSON `{\"Code\":\"ForbiddenError\",\"Message\":\"Missing read access to project id <id>, or the project does not exist [...]\"}`; PATCH and DELETE mostly answer 400 text/plain `Missing update access to project id <id>, or the project does not exist [...]` (env vars, columns and environments keep the 403 JSON form); prompts and functions answer 400 JSON `{\"Code\":\"BadRequestError\",\"Message\":\"Prompt does not exist or you do not have access [...]\"}`; ACLs answer 400 text/plain; event insert, fetch, summarize and restore on a missing experiment, dataset or project log answer the 403 JSON form; `DELETE /v1/service_token/{id}` answers 400 text/plain `Service token not found`; `POST /v1/function/{id}/invoke` answers 404 `Function not found (searching for {...})`. An anonymous GET of a project that exists returns the same 403 message, so the class covers a permission denial too and is named for both. The spec declares only status-wide 400 and 403 responses with no schema. `GET /v1/column` on a scoping project that is gone answers the same 403 JSON form (observed 2026-11-13: a random project id, and a just-deleted project with `subtype=experiment`, `Missing read access to project experiment id <id>, or the project experiment does not exist`); other scopes of a just-deleted project answer 200 with no objects. Feedback operations answer 200 for a missing id and are left out.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.braintrust#NotFoundOrForbidden",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "message": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String"
          }
        },
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#error": "client",
          "smithy.api#httpError": 404,
          "smithy.api#documentation": "The object does not exist, or the caller may not access it: Braintrust answers both with the same message (\"\u2026, or the <type> does not exist\").",
          "com.distilled.openapi#errorMatchers": [
            {
              "status": 403,
              "message": {
                "includes": "does not exist"
              }
            },
            {
              "status": 400,
              "message": {
                "includes": "does not exist"
              }
            },
            {
              "status": 400,
              "message": {
                "includes": "Service token not found"
              }
            },
            {
              "status": 404,
              "message": {
                "includes": "not found"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
